---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" path="/privacy-policy/" trail={[{ name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy-policy/" }]}
  description="How IT Code Lab handles personal data under India's DPDP Act and the GDPR. Cookie-less analytics only.">
  <article class="wrap section max-w-3xl">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede speakable mt-4">We collect only what you send us through our forms, and we use it only to reply to you.</p>
    <div class="prose-lab mt-10">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>Name, email, company and message when you submit a form. Forms are protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, which may process technical signals to detect bots.</p>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>To respond to your inquiry and, if you request it, to give you early access. We do not sell personal data.</p>
      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>This site sets no tracking cookies. Where analytics are enabled we use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookie-less and does not track individuals across sites.</p>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and, where applicable, the GDPR, you may request access, correction or erasure of your data, and withdraw consent at any time. Use the contact page to make a request.</p>
      <h2>Retention and processors</h2>
      <p>Inquiries are stored in a managed Postgres database and kept only as long as needed to handle the inquiry. Processors include Cloudflare (form handling, analytics) and our database provider.</p>
      <h2>Inbound contacts and suppression</h2>
      <p>If you contact us, your email domain is added to our internal suppression list so that our own outreach tools never contact you.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
